The Android and desktop interfaces may contain code adapted from OpenSCL4
(https://github.com/SckraT/OpenSCL4), licensed GPL-3.0-or-later. Files adapted
from OpenSCL4 keep their original copyright headers; changes are noted in the
file header or in the commit that introduces them.

The desktop interface of this product keeps the OpenSCL4 name and is presented
as OpenSCL4 2.0. Its Slint tree in `desktop/ui` is vendored from OpenSCL4 commit
01276e08 (https://github.com/SckraT/OpenSCL4), GPL-3.0-or-later. Changes and
adaptations are recorded in `desktop/ui/SOURCE.md`.

The core (`core/`) also adapts protocol and device data from the same OpenSCL4
project, under GPL-3.0-or-later:

- the A3062 `03 87` equalizer command body layout and the A3062 `01 01`
  equalizer state offsets, adapted from
  `lib/src/devices/soundcore/a3062/packets/outbound.rs`,
  `lib/src/devices/soundcore/a3062/packets/inbound/state_update.rs` and
  `lib/src/devices/soundcore/common/structures/equalizer_configuration.rs`;
- the A3062 equalizer preset table (ids, English names and ten-band curves) and
  the eight visible band frequencies, adapted from
  `lib/src/devices/soundcore/a3062/modules/equalizer.rs` and
  `lib/i18n/en/openscq30-lib.ftl`;
- the A3062 remaining-settings block at `01 01` state body 67..87 and the
  settings write command bodies (`04 81` button double press, `06 82` ambient
  sound mode cycle, `10 82` low battery prompt, `02 86` Dolby audio, `01 FF`
  LDAC, `0B 84` dual connections, `01 86` auto power off, `20 82` limit high
  volume, `20 81` limit high volume refresh rate, `01 84` side tone and
  `01 AE` ambient sound mode voice prompt), adapted from
  `lib/src/devices/soundcore/a3062/packets/inbound/state_update.rs`,
  `lib/src/devices/soundcore/a3062/packets/outbound.rs`,
  `lib/src/devices/soundcore/a3062/modules/flag.rs`,
  `lib/src/devices/soundcore/common/modules/flag.rs`,
  `lib/src/devices/soundcore/common/packet/outbound.rs` and
  `lib/src/devices/soundcore/common/packet/outbound/set_ambient_sound_mode_cycle.rs`,
  `.../dual_connections.rs`, `.../set_auto_power_off.rs` and
  `.../set_limit_high_volume.rs`;
- the OpenSCL4 transfer-profile format (`name` plus `volumeAdjustments`), its
  serialization in both directions (profile import and export) and its
  `scaled_to_device` decibel-to-band rounding rule for profile import, adapted
  from `lib/src/api/equalizer_profiles.rs`, and the import preview statuses
  (new, replaces, wrong band count, out of range) from
  `lib/src/client/equalizer.rs`;
- the A3949 equalizer block at state body 32..44, which is recorded as a
  deferred limitation (not implemented), from
  `lib/src/devices/soundcore/a3949/packets/inbound/state_update.rs` and
  `lib/src/devices/soundcore/a3949/state.rs`.

The Rust implementations in `core/` are this project's own; the adapted data and
its evidence are recorded in `.scratch/windows-eq-presets/`,
`.scratch/windows-settings-import/` and in the commits that introduce them.
